                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Correct. If there are equal moles of acid and base in a titration, then the solution is at the equivalence point, identified by a mid-range pH and extreme changes in pH around the equivalence point."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "f44d3dc6fd28438d9982f030f6710097",
                    "type": "p"
